emysa-tgcall (Phase 5 prototype)

The call-signaling sequencing (requestCall/acceptCall/confirmCall/discardCall,
signaling-blob relay, one-call-at-a-time busy decline, NTgCalls EXTERNAL-audio
usage, the playback-on-microphone quirk and relay-to-RTCServer mapping) follows
the approach documented and implemented in foobar26/tg2sip (Apache-2.0,
Copyright 2026 Frank Egger), commit fab2613. No source files were copied; the
code here is a re-implementation with a different structure. tg2sip's SIP/PJSUA2
layer is intentionally not used.

Runtime dependencies keep their own licenses:
  ntgcalls (NTgCalls, pytgcalls/ntgcalls)   - see https://github.com/pytgcalls/ntgcalls
  pyrogram 2.0.106                          - LGPL-3.0
MarshalX/tgcalls (LGPL-3.0) was inspected for research only; nothing from it is used.
